    "https://jobs.keldair.com/uindy/Faculty/jobs/101949/assistant-professor-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure- Track",
      "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading Assistant Professor, Tenure- Track Indianapolis, IN 46227 Posted: 10/08/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Faculty Pay: Depends upon skills and experience Department: Department of Clinical Psychology Experience: Mid-Level Apply Job Description The University of Indianapolis’ Department of Clinical Psychology (DCP) is growing and seeking a faculty member at the Assistant Professor level beginning in Fall 2027. This is a full-time, tenure-track position within our APA-accredited PsyD program. The successful applicant for this position will be able to demonstrate outstanding commitment to doctoral teaching and dissertation research mentorship. Any specialty area of interest/expertise in Clinical or Counseling Psychology is open. Additional duties include developing a program of research that engages graduate students, participating in ongoing program development within the PsyD program, and serving on faculty and university committees. The area of research interest is open, but the successful candidate’s area of scholarship should lend itself well to the development of a program of applied or basic research with the potential to make a significant contribution to the literature. Furthermore, candidates should bring a strong desire to apply their research expertise to chairing and mentoring student dissertations. The program supports many project types, including: traditional quantitative, qualitative, program development/evaluation, integrative/theoretical, and empirical single-case study design dissertation projects. The PsyD program fully promotes and furthers the value of diversity. UIndy is looking for candidates with a demonstrated commitment to and success working in a variety of different communities. Applicants who can demonstrate a history of effective mentoring of students from underrepresented backgrounds will be particularly competitive. We offer opportunities for faculty, staff, and students to participate in College- and Department-level diversity committees. In addition, we are home to professional organizations. The DCP is located within an academic unit that offers an APA-accredited PsyD program in clinical psychology; MS/MA degrees in Psychology, Mental Health Counseling, and Social Work; MA specialization in Art Therapy; and BS degrees in Psychology and Social Work. The doctoral program, which has adopted a practitioner-scholar model, typically enrolls 30-40 students per year and offers 7 concentrations, including Adult Psychopathology and Psychotherapy, Health Psychology & Behavioral Medicine, Neuropsychology, Community Psychology and Social Change, Assessment, Child and adolescent psychology and a Generalist track. Preference will be given to applicants from an APA-accredited doctoral program in clinical or counseling psychology who are licensed as a psychologist or license-eligible. ABDs and doctoral candidates currently completing internship will be considered with the expectation of degree completion prior to starting the position. UIndy DCP faculty are encouraged to actively engage in provision of direct clinical services to maintain clinical proficiency. Applicants are asked to submit a list of at least three professional references, a curriculum vita, a cover letter speaking to their qualifications in relation to the position responsibilities, and a statement reflecting on how they infuse diversity into their teaching and scholarship. The positions are open until filled with the review of applications to begin immediately. The University of Indianapolis is an accredited, private, comprehensive university whose motto is “Education for Service.” Ranked in the top tier of Midwest universities by U.S. News & World Report, the campus is situated in the 12th largest city in the United States. It is within a 10- minute drive of what Forbes magazine lists as one of “America’s Best Downtowns”, where the potential for networking includes a rich social and intellectual confluence of professionals, artists, and cultural/educational events. Indianapolis consistently ranks as having one of the lowest costs of living amongst major cities in the US and boasts affordable housing. Job Responsibilities: ● Teach dynamic, interactive, and engaging graduate courses. ● Supervise doctoral dissertations. ● Develop a program of research/scholarship that involves students. ● Serve on departmental, college, and/or university-wide committees. Qualifications: ● PhD or PsyD in Psychology, Counseling, or related field (Required) ● Experience teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level (Preferred) ● Be licensed or license-eligible as a Psychologist at the doctoral level. Required Documents: ● Unofficial Transcripts ● CV/Resume ● Cover Letter ● (Optional) Sample syllabi and/or past teaching evaluations Hard Skills: ● PhD or PsyD in Psychology, Counseling, or related field ● (Preferred) Experience teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level Company Description Thank you for your interest in the University of Indianapolis! The University is a private, comprehensive teaching university located on 65 acres just minutes from downtown Indianapolis. With more than 700 faculty and staff, it is a place where you can become part of a close-knit campus community that emphasizes the importance of community partnerships in the future growth of the University. UIndy’s mission is to prepare its graduates for effective, responsible, and articulate membership in the complex societies in which they live and serve and for excellence and leadership in their personal and professional lives. The motto of \"Education for Service\" provides the foundation for our work to better our communities, both near and far. As University employees, we know the work we do is important to our students and our communities. To accomplish our mission, we welcome talented, civic-minded, and diverse individuals from all career levels to help maintain our high standards of excellence and quality. If you want to join our dynamic environment and experience hard work, creativity, and teamwork, we welcome your application! The University of Indianapolis is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, age, color, religion, national origin, disability, citizenship status, military status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. The University of Indianapolis does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment and admission as required by Title IX. Benefits Medical Insurance Vision Insurance Dental Insurance Life Insurance Tuition Discount Retirement Savings Plan - 403B Employee Discounts & Services Free Parking Onsite Health & Wellness Center For more information about the benefits of being a staff or faculty member at UIndy, visit our Benefits site. Apply The University of Indianapolis is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, age, color, religion, national origin, disability, citizenship status, military status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. The University of Indianapolis does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment and admission as required by Title IX. Privacy Policy Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.keldair.com/uindy/Staff/jobs/101894/vp-of-advancement": {
      "title": "VP of Advancement",
      "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading VP of Advancement Indianapolis, IN 46227 Posted: 10/04/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Full-time Pay: Depends upon skills and experience Department: Advancement Experience: Senior Apply Job Description The University of Indianapolis seeks a bold, entrepreneurial, and relationship-driven advancement leader to build upon a period of exceptional momentum and help shape the University’s next era of impact. Over the past three years, under the leadership of President Dr. Tanuja Singh, UIndy has strengthened its financial position, achieved sustained fundraising success, expanded academic and workforce initiatives, and forged ambitious partnerships—including an Innovation and Entrepreneurship Program with Perry Township Schools that will bring Indiana’s first high school located on a university campus to UIndy. The launch of UIndy Online, significant investments in engineering, nursing, honors education, and student success, and a growing portfolio of corporate and community partnerships reflect a University that is confident in its direction and ready to translate its momentum into even greater philanthropic support. Reporting directly to the President, the Vice President for University Advancement will serve as a key member of the President’s Cabinet and an active participant in strategic decisions affecting the University. UIndy seeks an energetic, active fundraiser who will spend the majority of their time engaging, cultivating, and soliciting donors; securing significant philanthropic investments; and building enduring relationships that advance the University’s mission and strategic priorities. Working closely with the President, senior leadership, and the Board of Trustees, and supported by an experienced advancement team responsible for the unit’s day-to-day operations, the Vice President will lead UIndy’s overall fundraising strategy, strengthen its culture of philanthropy, and develop external alliances that expand the University’s visibility, reach, and financial resources. The position will involve local, regional and national travel. Position Details: The Vice President of Advancement, reporting directly to President Dr. Tanuja Singh, serves as a key leadership team member of the President's Cabinet and an active participant in strategic decisions affecting UIndy. This role requires an active, front-line fundraiser with a primary focus on relationship building, donor engagement, cultivation, and solicitation. The Vice President will spend the majority of their time out of the office including on regional and national travel, building high-value relationships, securing major philanthropic gifts from individual donors and stewarding those relationships, and driving the University's overall fundraising strategy. While operational advancement staff manage day-to-day administrative unit functions, the Vice President works in close partnership with senior leadership, the President, and the Board of Trustees to forge key external alliances that expand UIndy's visibility, philanthropic reach, and overall financial resources. Essential Functions Front-Line Fundraising & Major Gifts: Serve as the major fundraiser for the University alongside the president, actively building, managing, and advancing a portfolio of major gift prospects to regularly secure seven-figure and higher philanthropic gifts from individual and institutional donors. Senior Leadership Collaboration: Partner closely with the President, Provost, Deans, Athletic Director, and senior executive management to collaboratively strategize, cultivate, and solicit major gifts across key academic and athletic priorities. Board & Trustee Engagement: Serve as the official staff liaison for the Board of Trustees Advancement Committee, actively engaging board members in major donor cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship initiatives. Campaign & Private Foundation Strategy: Develop and execute comprehensive fundraising strategies that encompass major gifts, planned giving, private foundation grants, and multi-year comprehensive campaigns. Relationship Building & Stewardship: Design and implement high-touch cultivation and stewardship programs to foster deep, long-term relationships with individual, corporate, and foundation donors. Financial & Compliance Partnership: Collaborate with the Chief Financial Officer on financial alignment and with the Office of General Counsel to ensure all gift agreements and fundraising activities follow federal, state, and local regulations. Alumni Association Representation: Serve as a key spokesperson for the University to the UIndy Alumni Association, enhancing engagement and a culture of philanthropy across the UIndy Greyhound alumni community. Institutional Alignment: Demonstrate respectful, ethical, and responsible behavior in alignment with University policies, procedures, and rules. Requirements & Qualifications Experience & Track Record: 10+ years of professional experience in higher education or major non-profit advancement, with a proven track record as a successful fundraiser. Proven track record of securing major philanthropic gifts (seven figures or higher) from individual donors. Proven track record of relationship building and management, with demonstrated success in identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding high-net-worth individual donors. Proven track record of working collaboratively with senior management (Presidents, Deans, Vice Presidents) to prepare for, execute, and close major gift solicitations. Strong understanding of complex gift agreements, structured giving, and their long-term impact on the university. Preferred Qualifications: Successful experience leading or co-leading a multi-year comprehensive campaign within a higher education institution. Demonstrated experience successfully managing board relations and engaging trustees in front-line fundraising activities. Proven track record in private foundation cultivation and solicitation, including relationship building with program officers and securing institutional grants. Education & Credentials: Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree or higher preferred. Certified Fund Raising Executive (CFRE) designation preferred. Competencies & Key Characteristics: Front-Line Focus: Energetic, self-motivated external fundraiser who thrives on face-to-face donor engagement and relationship building. Persuasive Communication: Superior written and verbal communication skills, with an ability to compellingly articulate UIndy's mission to diverse audiences. Strategic Partnering: Ability to work seamlessly with senior executives, trustees, campus leaders, faculty, and volunteer leadership to execute sophisticated cultivation and solicitation strategies. Independence & Initiative: High degree of self-direction, organizational skills, and attention to detail, capable of driving major gift pipelines forward without heavy administrative oversight. Integrity & Passion: High ethical standards, professional discretion, and a genuine passion for higher education and UIndy's mission. Company Description Located in Indianapolis, the University of Indianapolis (UIndy) is a nationally recognized, United Methodist Church-affiliated institution that serves over 4,200 main-campus students, including more than 1,300 graduate students. Guided by over 500 accessible faculty members who foster high student-faculty interaction, UIndy offers an intimate learning environment with an average class size of 16 and a 12:1 student-to-faculty ratio across its 90+ undergraduate, 40+ graduate, and five doctoral programs—notably producing more clinical psychologists than any other university in Indiana and featuring the state's only neonatal nurse practitioner program. Beyond academic excellence and a diverse campus community where 33% of students represent international and minority populations from over 60 countries and 40 states, UIndy boasts a powerhouse NCAA Division II athletics program. Featuring 23 varsity teams, the Greyhounds demonstrate athletic and academic excellence, earning 13 consecutive top-20 finishes in the Learfield Directors' Cup and securing 19 conference championships in a two-year span, while its 600+ student-athletes simultaneously achieved a combined 3.52 GPA and 405 Academic All-GLVC honors. Our Mission The University of Indianapolis champions lifelong learning through relevant and innovative education that fosters experiential learning, diverse perspectives, service for impact, and a global mindset. Our Vision The University of Indianapolis will be the institution of choice for a diverse group of learners who wish to engage with the world and enrich their lives through relevant and impactful education, and are empowered to transform the world with their knowledge and skills—Anywhere. Anytime. For life. Benefits Medical Insurance Vision Insurance Dental Insurance Tuition Discount Retirement Savings Plan - 403B Paid Vacation and Sick Time Accruals Paid Holiday time and additional University days off Employee Discounts & Services Free Parking Onsite Health & Wellness Center Apply The University of Indianapolis is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, age, color, religion, national origin, disability, citizenship status, military status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. The University of Indianapolis does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment and admission as required by Title IX. Privacy Policy Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.keldair.com/uindy/Staff/jobs/101814/general-maintenance-technician": {
      "title": "General Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Careers | Job Application Empty heading General Maintenance Technician Indianapolis, IN 46227 Posted: 10/02/2026 Deadline: Open until filled Employment: Full-time, Non-exempt Pay: $18.00 - $20.00 per Hour Department: Facilities Management Experience: Entry-Level Apply Job Description Service oriented with general knowledge of building maintenance. This employee must have basic knowledge of carpentry, electrical, plumbing, and mechanical systems. This employee will respond to work orders on a tablet with our work order system. REQUIREMENTS/MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Experience 1–2 years’ experience in building maintenance preferred Education High School diploma or GED required Licenses/Certifications/Credentials Valid driver’s license is required ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: This is an essential staff position that may be required to report to work when the university is closed or during inclement weather when a state-of-emergency has been declared. This position is part of the on-call rotation and will have to help with snow removal if needed. This employee will work with all trades to assist with work orders or projects as needed. Will be working on the general work orders, such as replacing ceiling tiles, light bulbs, and changing air filters in HVAC units. Follow the guidance and direction of supervisor(s). Demonstrate respectful, ethical, responsible behavior. Abide by the University’s policies, procedures, and rules. Perform employee responsibilities as detailed in employee handbooks and policies. Demonstrate regular and predictable attendance and punctuality. Other duties, including special projects, as required or assigned. Overtime may be required at times, vacation approval may be limited during peak activity periods. Company Description Thank you for your interest in the University of Indianapolis! The University is a private, comprehensive teaching university located on 65 acres just minutes from downtown Indianapolis. With more than 700 facult